jq's values, the millions of small blocks a big input parses into, come from
livejq's own allocator (src/heap/heap.c) instead of malloc: size classes in
64 KB spans per thread, with no header per block, handing empty spans back to
the system. only the allocations of values move, all of them made and freed
in this file; jv_mem_alloc stays malloc, as jq frees some of its blocks with
free().

